# PlasticOS Version Bump — Mandatory

**Skill SSOT:** `skills/plasticos-odoo-version-bump/SKILL.md`

## Never ask

Do **not** ask the user whether to bump a module version. If a `plasticos_*`
change must reach a running DB, bump that module's `__manifest__.py` version in
the same change set.

## Never forget

Odoo skips reload when the version is unchanged. Editing migrate scripts under
an already-applied version is a no-op — bump to the next `19.0.X.Y.Z` and add a
matching `migrations/<new_version>/` folder.

## Scoped upgrade only

After a bump, upgrade **only** that module:

```bash
make update m=<bumped_module>
```

Do **not** `make update-all` or `-u` unrelated solid modules. Staging carries a
large `res.partner` set — full-stack reloads waste time and hide the real fault.

## Task router

| Change | Action |
|---|---|
| Python / XML / data / security / hooks / migrations in module M | Bump M; `make update m=M` |
| Multiple modules changed | Bump each changed module; `-u` comma-list of **those only** |
| Tests/docs/CI only | No bump |
